{"step_index":257,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-28T02:27:49Z","thinking":"**Analyzing the provided details**\n\nOkay, I'm now processing the input: \"배현명 대성이앤지 6033094589 문한석 46721 부산광역시 강서구 유통단지1로 41 (대저2동, 128동 114호) 도장 및 기타 피막처리업 135511-0112454 12월 제조업\". I am dissecting each element to understand its significance.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":false,"Summary":"Script to batch search biz numbers using duckduckgo or web search.","UserFacing":false},"CodeContent":"import urllib.request\nimport urllib.parse\nimport json\nimport re\nimport time\n\nwith open(r'C:\\Users\\lg\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\6849e270-cdbb-4526-97ab-99f7d77523f7\\scratch\\biz_err_targets.json', 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    targets = json.load(f)\n\ndef validate_biz_no(val):\n    clean = re.sub(r'[^0-9]', '', str(val))\n    if len(clean) != 10:\n        return False, clean\n    weights = [1, 3, 7, 1, 3, 7, 1, 3, 5]\n    digits = [int(c) for c in clean]\n    s = sum(digits[i] * weights[i] for i in range(8))\n    s += (digits[8] * 5) // 10 + (digits[8] * 5) % 10\n    chk = (10 - (s % 10)) % 10\n    return digits[9] == chk, clean\n\nprint(f\"Loaded {len(targets)} targets.\")\n","Description":"Batch lookup script","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\lg\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\6849e270-cdbb-4526-97ab-99f7d77523f7\\scratch\\batch_lookup.py","toolAction":"Creating batch lookup script","toolSummary":"Run batch_lookup.py"}}]}
